GH issue: https://github.com/clankercode/lsp-openplanet/issues/56 (gh-56)

Verified still open 2026-08-24 @ 728c30d: no `unused_callbacks` key exists in
`src/config.rs`; the exemption list is hardcoded (`OPENPLANET_CALLBACKS`,
src/analysis/unused.rs:44+).

## DECISIONS (do not re-litigate)

1. **Implement now, despite the issue's "do not implement until a real FP is
   observed"**: the issue itself records a real one (MLHook name-reflection
   dispatch of `OnCounterUpdate`), and gh-55 adds a second consumer of the list
   (param exemptions). User asked for it in this batch.
2. **Key**: top-level `unused_callbacks = ["OnCounterUpdate", "OnThing*"]` in
   `.openplanet-lsp.toml` / user global config — the config file is flat (no
   sections); it sits beside `source_paths` / `ignore_paths`.
3. **Additive, never replacing**: entries extend `OPENPLANET_CALLBACKS`. There is
   no "disable defaults" switch (contrast `shortcut_disable_default_namespaces`)
   — dropping engine callbacks from the exemption list only manufactures FPs.
4. **Pattern syntax**: literal names plus a single `*` wildcard (prefix `Foo*`,
   suffix `*Update`, and bare `*` matching everything). NOT full glob, NOT regex.
   Rationale: smallest surface that covers reflective-dispatch naming
   conventions; no new dependency.
5. **Match target**: unqualified names of **free functions declared at file top
   level** — same population the hardcoded list applies to. Class methods are out
   of scope (MLHook dispatches free functions); revisit only on a real FP.
6. **Precedence**: standard ladder — workspace `.openplanet-lsp.toml` wins over
   user global when both set the key (same rule as `warnings_as_errors`). Lists
   do not merge across levels; the winning file's list is the list.
7. **Docs**: README config block + CHANGELOG entry.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Variants: literal name exempts; prefix `On*`; suffix `*Update`; bare `*`;
non-matching name still warns; hardcoded defaults still exempt when the key is
set; class method with a matching name still warns (decision 5); workspace file
overrides user global; malformed values (non-array, non-string entries) ignored
without panicking; empty list is a no-op.

## Lane
Lane A, step 2 of 2 — depends on gh-55 (shared files: src/analysis/unused.rs;
gh-55 adds the param consumer of this list). Files: src/config.rs,
src/analysis/unused.rs, README.md, CHANGELOG.md, tests/.